{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1454214-i-d-like-to-have-feedback-on-a-custom-totem","id":1454214,"title":"I'd like to have feedback on a custom Totem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-04T10:29:54-07:00","id":1454214,"title":"I'd like to have feedback on a custom Totem","content":"Hey guys, I'd like to have some feedback on a custom Totem that I would like to introduce in my group. What do you think? Too powerful, not thematically focused enough, etc.? TIA<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rainbow (Totem of Wisdom)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Background Cost:</b> 7<br /> <br /> Rainbow is an ancient spirit that has been closely associated with Unicorn in recent decades. In the course of history, rainbows have meant many different things to different peoples; in some cultures, they bridged the worlds of spirit and matter (or the divine and mortal), in others, they represented hope, unity, peace, or a great transformations and, again in others, they were sometimes even seen as heralds of doom. Rainbow as a spirit is a bringer of hope, unity, and positive social change. Likewise, Garou who dedicate themselves to Rainbow strive to bring about unity and solidarity between the spiritual and the material, between the strong and the weak, between the bold and the meek, between the wanted and the outcast. Often, Rainbow tasks them with improving the diplomatic relations between groups that are very different\u2014whether mortals, Garou, or spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>Individual Traits:</b> Rainbow\u2019s children gain two points of Honor Renown. In addition, they can use the Gift: Brother\u2019s Scent once per day.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Traits:</b> Rainbow\u2019s packs can call on one dot of Charisma, one dot of Appearance, two dots of Etiquette and two dots of Leadership.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Children of Rainbow must work towards positive social change at least once a month. This could take the form of direct support, like helping out in a soup kitchen or a local shelter for homeless youths, or it could take the form of a more \u2018hands-off\u2019 approach, such as organizing fundraising events among the social elite. Improving the relationship between a Sept and the spirit world counts for the purpose of this Ban as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T12:53:07-07:00","id":1454228,"title":"","content":"Even for a 7 dot Totem, it feels like a bit much. Brother's Scent isn't a Gift that you generally spam a lot of, so the once per day restriction probably isn't going to be felt (and a pack following Rainbow would appreciate having it, but presumably not need to rely on it anyway). Two Attribute dots and four Ability dots for the Pack Traits is pretty hefty, and the system doesn't really reward much in the way of multiple social characters rolling at once (like it does with combat) so only one pack member getting the boost at a time isn't that big of a restriction. The Ban is also rather generous as far as these things go.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, overall this is a pretty generous Totem mechanically. I'd say you need to do some adjustment towards increasing the drawbacks (price, ban) or reducing the bonuses.<br /> <br /> That all said, it's conceptually solid, and good start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T13:56:57-07:00","id":1454234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1454214-i-d-like-to-have-feedback-on-a-custom-totem?p=1454228#post1454228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even for a 7 dot Totem, it feels like a bit much. Brother's Scent isn't a Gift that you generally spam a lot of, so the once per day restriction probably isn't going to be felt (and a pack following Rainbow would appreciate having it, but presumably not need to rely on it anyway). Two Attribute dots and four Ability dots for the Pack Traits is pretty hefty, and the system doesn't really reward much in the way of multiple social characters rolling at once (like it does with combat) so only one pack member getting the boost at a time isn't that big of a restriction. The Ban is also rather generous as far as these things go.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, overall this is a pretty generous Totem mechanically. I'd say you need to do some adjustment towards increasing the drawbacks (price, ban) or reducing the bonuses.<br /> <br /> That all said, it's conceptually solid, and good start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the feedback, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>!<br /> <br /> Hm, I'll have to think about some nerfing then. Maybe it would be better to put the Gift into the Pack Trait category, lose one of the attribute dots, and increase the Ban frequency to once a week?<br /> <br /> Do you have any suggestions, by any chance? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T15:02:58-07:00","id":1454247,"title":"","content":"I'd drop the Honor bonus (I find them a silly waste myself, even if common, since they're one time bonuses that you can easily get via playing the game anyway), drop the restriction on Brother's Scent (leave it as the Individual bonus, it's only a Rank 1 Gift, and it's one of those things that can be useful for members of the pack less geared to get maximum benefit from the Totem), and drop Appearance (it fits thematically with rainbows, but mechanically it's doesn't do what you have Rainbow doing).<br /> <br /> I think the Ban needs to be more significant rather than more time based (also time based stuff puts weird pressures on the ST). While the things the Ban has you do right now are thematic, they're not really changing anything, they're just helping people get by until change can happen. Change takes time, so I'd probably switch gears to a two part Ban:<br /> <br /> 1) They have to be actively engaged in efforts that result in concrete changes, even if they take a long time to realize. Rainbow's children don't just help at shelters, they get shelters built. They push the passage of laws to allow community programs that we know decrease homelesses, drug abuse, by helping people instead of punishing them, etc. This is long time frame stuff, so let Rainbow be patient as long as the pack is engaged and working on such things.<br /> <br /> 2) To put something a bit more &quot;gameable&quot; on the table and to have something more specific for the pack: At least once a season, they have to successfully tell a tale at a Moot that sways those at a Sept towards seeing positive social change as fighting the Wyrm. This can be within their home Sept to convince more packs to engage with local efforts, impressing visiting packs/Garou to take things to heart when moving on, or going to other Septs and helping to spread the message. This puts a lot of pressure on the players to be proactive with smaller victories while working on #1. This also is a good place for narrative drama as the PCs are going to have to buck traditional Garou thinking and probably make some enemies in the process. &quot;Sure, the Sept killed a dozen fomori in an attack on Wyrm infested crack house, but we stopped hundreds of humans from becoming fomori in the first place by getting them off of tainted drugs,&quot; is logically a strong argument for Rainbow's ways, but those warriors don't want to be disrespected like that. Put that Charisma, Etiquette, and Leadership to good use.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T17:23:43-07:00","id":1454256,"title":"","content":"I think usually it is totems of Respect that provide Honor, and totems of Wisdom provide Wisdom renown. This may not be a universal rule, but it's definitely a general one. That you put the totem in Wisdom but gave renown as Honor may indicate you need to rethink the purpose of the totem and where it really fits - Wisdom or Honor. You may be wanting it to do too many things.<br /> <br /> I also think it's a good idea to consider the totem in all historical time periods and with all breeds. Is the way you constructed the totem make sense for Garou who lived during the Stone Age, the Bronze Age, the Classical era, the Middle Ages, etc.? How would Garou in a Stone Age setting where most people are in small migratory bands work towards that ban? Or in a small farming village during the Iron Age? It seems to me that something as universal as the rainbow would have appealed to lupus Garou, yet what does something so human centric as &quot;positive social change&quot; mean to them? If they are living as a wolf pack in the forest how can they follow the ban? Many poorly written official totems fail this test, but I think it's an important one.<br /> <br /> Also, what is considered to be &quot;positive social change&quot; can change from time to time, sometimes even in a very short time period. In that case, what one pack of Rainbow might work towards could be what another pack of Rainbow work against (perhaps even in the exact same time and place). I don't think that is what you intended. So you may want to rethink and tweak that. Personally, I wouldn't go too far into the realm of human politics, but that goes against the universal and ancient nature of Rainbow. Think mythically more instead of politically.<br /> <br /> I know you mentioned that things like &quot;improving the relationship between a Sept and the spirit world&quot; counts, but to me this would be a weak ban. It's like saying the ban is to fight the Wyrm. It's something most Garou are going to do anyway so it doesn't really have an impact on the behavior of a group of PCs. There's also another argument against that in my opinion. You are taking something that is ultimately about members of a pack, but now turning it into an issue for the sept. Yet pack members can certainly control their own behavior, but they can't control the behavior of others, even those that belong to the same sept. And what about anruth packs that travel from sept to sept. How would they be affected?<br /> <br /> In my opinion, the best bans are something that occasionally forces PC behavior - to either do a specific thing or refrain from it. So if you want to emphasize a unit or connection between the earth and the heavens (the material and the spiritual), you should think about things that they can directly control. Things that either they must do in certain circumstances or things they can never do. does that mean a higher chiminage requirement? Performance of certain rites at certain times or occasions? A specific kind of quest they must do every so often? Never attempting to deceive a spirit? Never fight one unless it is a Triatic spirit like a Bane or Pattern Spider? Must they always find an additional spirit in whatever region they are in, &quot;adopt&quot; it and keep it happy? Reviewing a sourcebook like Umbra: the Velvet Shadow or Axis Mundi may give you ideas on making a more concrete ban that fits the &quot;uniting the spiritual and material&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or could it be something that is provoked as a result of rainbows appearing. An activity they must perform after they see a rainbow? Or after any heavy rain? Something they need to do during a rainstorm so that rainbows will appear? What happens if a pack mostly lives in a desert environment where rainbows are rare? What about artifical rainbows as a result of glass windows or prisms?<br /> <br /> You may also want to think about bans that are less about the purpose of the totem, and more about the nature of the totem. Maybe a component of the ban is for the Garou to not wear any colors not found in the rainbow. No whites, blacks, grays, for example. This may become important not just for clothes, but items like fetishes and technological devices, or putting on camoflauge or other make up. I wouldn't make this the primary ban of the totem, but it could be additional flavor.<br /> <br /> I think there are a lot of bad bans in the official published pack totems. Some are way too specific. Some put too much on the PCs or STs to come up during play. Or don't affect personal behavior at all. Or simply can't be done outside the assumptions of modern civilization when most of the Garou's existence was when humanity was much more primitive and extensive. So I hope whatever ban you decide avoids things I think are common mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T21:45:25-07:00","id":1454261,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the fantastic suggestions/feedback, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> (again) and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>!<br /> <br /> I'll have to mull this over for a day or two, before I can decide where to go with this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1454214-i-d-like-to-have-feedback-on-a-custom-totem?p=1454256#post1454256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think it's a good idea to consider the totem in all historical time periods and with all breeds. Is the way you constructed the totem make sense for Garou who lived during the Stone Age, the Bronze Age, the Classical era, the Middle Ages, etc.? How would Garou in a Stone Age setting where most people are in small migratory bands work towards that ban? Or in a small farming village during the Iron Age? It seems to me that something as universal as the rainbow would have appealed to lupus Garou, yet what does something so human centric as &quot;positive social change&quot; mean to them? If they are living as a wolf pack in the forest how can they follow the ban? Many poorly written official totems fail this test, but I think it's an important one.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is valuable advice, so thank you. However, I seem to remember that Totems can and do change with the times, and that Rainbow of the Stone Age wouldn't necessarily have to be the same as today's Rainbow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T02:25:21-07:00","id":1454268,"title":"","content":"There's definitely Totems that have undergone massive changes over the centuries. There's also Totems that are rather young. The Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers esp. have lots of examples of both. The vast majority of City Fathers/Mothers, for example, are very young by this sort of consideration. Even most of the &quot;old&quot; ones aren't stretching back into paleolithic times, and have likely gone through some massive changes as their physical counterparts have changed (Consider how history would have impacted the City Totem of Rome even as an older example of a city that's been a major city for as long as Rome has been).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T00:58:09-07:00","id":1454676,"title":"","content":"I tried to integrate your feedback. By the way, the classification in the OP was erroneous. When I wrote up the totem originally, I had classified Rainbow as a Totem of Respect, but for some reason mistakenly changed it when copying it into the forum.<br /> <br /> So, do you think the revisions make it more balanced?<br /> <br /> =================================================<br /> <br /> <b>Rainbow (Totem of Respect)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Background Cost:</b> 7<br /> <br /> In the course of history, rainbows have meant many different things to different peoples. In most cultures, rainbows inspired awe and joy in those who witnessed them. For some, they bridged the worlds of spirit and matter (or the divine and mortal), for others, they represented hope, unity, peace, or a great transformations and, again for others, they were sometimes even seen as heralds of doom.<br /> <br /> Accordingly, Rainbow is an ancient spirit whose role in the spirit world changed during its long history. At the beginning of time, it united the material world with the deeper Umbra, allowing mortals to experience the beyond and glimpse all its possibilities. As the material world and the Velvet Shadow grew further apart over time, however, Rainbow\u2019s role has shifted away from actually uniting spirit and matter; instead, it started to represent the hope and joy of unity, the promise of blissfully reuniting those elements that have been sundered apart.<br /> <br /> In recent decades, Rainbow has been closely associated with Unicorn and is considered to be a bringer of hope, joy, unity, and positive change. Likewise, Garou who dedicate themselves to Rainbow strive to bring about unity and solidarity between the spiritual and the material, between the strong and the weak, between the bold and the meek, between the wanted and the outcast. Often, Rainbow tasks them with improving the diplomatic relations between groups that are very different\u2014whether mortals, Garou, or spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>Individual Traits:</b> Rainbow\u2019s children gain the Gift: Brother\u2019s Scent.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Traits:</b> Rainbow\u2019s packs can call on one dot of Charisma, two dots of Etiquette and two dots of Leadership.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Children of Rainbow must be actively engaged in long-term efforts that result in concrete positive social change. For Rainbow\u2019s children, it is not enough to help out directly, they have to improve upon the underlying causes for disunity and disenfranchisement, so that direct help becomes less necessary. For example, they do not just help out at homeless shelters, they have to work on getting homeless shelters built or to push the passage of laws that allow for community programs that decrease homelessness, drug abuse, etc.; they not only have to help saving their wolf kin from hunters, they have to work on long-term preservation efforts that reduce hostility from humans and increase the safety and freedom of wolf packs. Since these changes take time, Rainbow is very patient with its children.<br /> <br /> However, as a way to keep Rainbow\u2019s children accountable, they have to tell a tale at a Moot at least once a season that successfully sways those at a Sept towards seeing positive social change as fighting the Wyrm. This can be within their home Sept to convince more packs to engage with local efforts, impressing visiting packs or Garou to take things to heart when moving on, or going to other Septs and helping to spread the message.<br /> <br /> If the children of Rainbow enter the Spirit World, Rainbow requires them to take on ambassadorial duties. Not only do they have to display all the colors of the rainbow on their body in some form, they are also required to formally declare their presence to the spirits with a short ritual and to never initiate hostilities against spirits, unless they are attacked first.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T01:35:18-07:00","id":1454677,"title":"","content":"Nice, though you might want to add a caveat that the last part of the Ban doesn't extend to Banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}